#!/usr/bin/env bash
# The ONE classifier of INFRASTRUCTURE failures of a CI run (the job never started: account payments or spending limit; runner setup, a lost or shut-down runner, shallow fetch,
# network, auth, a 5xx from a service, a tool the runner lacks): a run that matches says nothing about the commit. Sourced (never run) by scripts/land-direct, whose red-check does
# not freeze landing on one (a code failure, an empty or unreadable log and an unreadable annotation still freeze). Protected set: weakening this list unfreezes a red main.
# `infra_re` is an ERE for `grep -E`, applied to the failed job's annotations and to the failed log. Ported from the originating project's scripts/infra-re.sh, with the account/billing annotations added.
infra_re='recent account payments have failed|spending limit|The job was not started|shallow update|Permission denied \(publickey\)|Internal Server Error|Bad Gateway|Service Unavailable|Gateway Time-?out|HTTP/[0-9.]+ 50[0-9]|error: 50[0-9]|status (code )?50[0-9]|RPC failed|early EOF|Could not resolve host|Temporary failure in name resolution|Connection (reset|timed out|refused)|TLS handshake timeout|No space left on device|runner has received a shutdown signal|lost communication with the server|E: (Unable to|Failed to fetch)|fatal: unable to access|fatal: could not read|Unable to (download|locate)|rate limit exceeded|is not installed'
